1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,080
This is TraceHarbor, built by Vengers for The Agent That Can Explain Why.

2
00:00:05,080 --> 00:00:10,550
This edited demonstration uses actual application captures, synthetic shipment records, and a synthetic narrator.

3
00:00:10,550 --> 00:00:16,411
We will inspect four working cases, then the receipts from a real local agent investigation.

4
00:00:16,961 --> 00:00:21,115
An operations analyst needs to understand a disputed temperature alert.

5
00:00:21,115 --> 00:00:26,099
The manifest, sensor readings, carrier events, and calibration records tell different stories.

6
00:00:26,099 --> 00:00:30,253
In this case, three calibrated readings exceed the stated limit.

7
00:00:30,253 --> 00:00:33,991
The original clear status stays visible as a contradiction.

8
00:00:33,991 --> 00:00:38,976
A nearby door event is an association, not proof of the cause.

9
00:00:39,526 --> 00:00:41,695
Now consider a different shipment.

10
00:00:41,695 --> 00:00:44,299
Its raw readings appear too warm.

11
00:00:44,299 --> 00:00:51,675
A confirmed calibration certificate records a sensor offset, and the corrected readings fall within the stated range.

12
00:00:51,675 --> 00:00:53,845
Independently calibrated reference observations agree.

13
00:00:53,845 --> 00:00:57,316
An expired certificate cannot replace the applicable one.

14
00:00:57,316 --> 00:01:01,656
The explanation is sensor bias, with its supporting evidence preserved.

15
00:01:02,206 --> 00:01:07,286
Open the evidence view to inspect the actual rows behind a finding.

16
00:01:07,286 --> 00:01:13,212
Stable record identifiers connect the explanation to the source, including the original reported values.

17
00:01:13,212 --> 00:01:15,752
Contradictions and rejected observations remain inspectable.

18
00:01:15,752 --> 00:01:20,832
The evidence strength is a transparent heuristic, not a probability of safety.

19
00:01:20,832 --> 00:01:23,796
The application does not authorize cargo release.

20
00:01:24,346 --> 00:01:29,332
The What If experiment tests whether the explanation survives without its supporting calibration.

21
00:01:29,332 --> 00:01:32,401
Withhold that evidence, and TraceHarbor recomputes the result.

22
00:01:32,401 --> 00:01:37,004
The sensor bias explanation becomes an abstention because the record is incomplete.

23
00:01:37,004 --> 00:01:43,141
This is a sensitivity check on the available evidence, not a prediction of a physical intervention.

24
00:01:43,691 --> 00:01:48,617
This shipment has only two of seven expected observations and a long sampling gap.

25
00:01:48,617 --> 00:01:53,190
A confident operator note and a pending calibration cannot fill those missing measurements.

26
00:01:53,190 --> 00:01:56,005
TraceHarbor abstains and asks for the missing evidence.

27
00:01:56,005 --> 00:02:00,227
It proposes a bounded next step rather than inventing a complete history.

28
00:02:00,777 --> 00:02:03,693
Here is the actual live agent investigation.

29
00:02:03,693 --> 00:02:07,442
The initial manifest and telemetry leave the result unresolved.

30
00:02:07,442 --> 00:02:11,608
The critic chooses to retrieve incidents and calibration through Zetaris.

31
00:02:11,608 --> 00:02:14,524
The agent then explains the sensor bias.

32
00:02:14,524 --> 00:02:17,440
Its calibration-withholding check returns to insufficient evidence.

33
00:02:17,440 --> 00:02:22,022
These model decisions change the available evidence and the computed conclusion.

34
00:02:22,572 --> 00:02:29,385
The fourth case is a normal control: the available observations remain within the fixture's stated range.

35
00:02:29,385 --> 00:02:31,514
Different records produce different conclusions.

36
00:02:31,514 --> 00:02:40,031
16 local tests pass, including a critic that retrieves missing calibration and changes an unresolved result into a supported explanation.

37
00:02:40,031 --> 00:02:45,141
Automated orchestration tests use mocked network transports; actual execution has separate receipts.

38
00:02:45,691 --> 00:02:54,639
A complete investigation now has three actual Nightshift model calls, 4 Zetaris reads, and 46 records consumed from the official World Model.

39
00:02:54,639 --> 00:02:57,486
The local Llama model uses structured decisions.

40
00:02:57,486 --> 00:03:01,147
The public website remains a clearly labeled synthetic sample.

41
00:03:01,147 --> 00:03:04,400
Reproducible source and execution receipts are on GitHub.

42
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:08,061
Our next validation is a real operations user study.
